SECTION 4: UNIFIED LISTING SYSTEM
======================================================================
Extend the existing listing system with four transaction types: SELL, SWAP,
BORROW, RENT. Use ONE unified listing model with a transaction_type field and
type-specific attributes. Do not create four separate systems.

Common fields: listing ID, seller ID, item name, category, description,
images, original purchase price, item age, condition, suggested fair price,
asking price, transaction type, availability status, creation date.

SELL: suggested fair price (from the existing engine), asking price, optional
PRIVATE minimum acceptable price, "willing to negotiate" flag. The private
minimum must NEVER appear in any public API response, listing JSON, frontend
HTML or buyer-facing screen. Buyers can request at the asking price, submit
an offer, and see whether negotiation is accepted. Sellers can accept, reject
or counteroffer. No competitive bidding in this phase.

SWAP: the item offered; categories/items the seller would accept; whether
multiple swap options are accepted. A buyer proposes a swap by choosing one of
their own listings or describing an exchange. A swap is valid only after both
parties accept.

BORROW (free lending): availability; min/max duration; collection location;
special conditions; optional refundable deposit. The borrower gives start
date, expected return date and an optional message; the owner accepts or
rejects. After acceptance the item is reserved for the agreed period. Track:
request, approval, collection confirmation, active borrowing, return
confirmation, completion.

RENT (separate from borrowing): rental price per day or agreed duration;
availability; min/max period; optional refundable deposit; collection location;
conditions. The renter selects dates and submits a request; the owner accepts
or rejects. Track: request, approval, reservation, collection, active rental,
return, completion.

No payment gateway. Payment and item inspection happen in person between
students. The app manages only requests, agreements, availability and confirmations.

