SECTION 5: PRICING AND NEGOTIATION
======================================================================
Preserve the existing pricing engine. For SELL listings keep three separate
concepts: suggested fair price (engine), asking price (seller), minimum
acceptable price (optional, private). Example: suggested Rs 3,000, asking
Rs 3,200, private minimum Rs 2,700; a buyer offers Rs 2,900; the seller
accepts, rejects or counters. Never reveal the minimum to buyers. Never
auto-accept an offer just because it exceeds the private minimum. The suggested
price is guidance, not mandatory. RENT uses rental pricing (not the resale
price), BORROW can be free, SWAP does not force a monetary price.

======================================================================
SECTION 6: TRANSACTION LIFECYCLES
======================================================================
Never mark an item sold, swapped, borrowed or returned just because a button is
clicked.
SELL: AVAILABLE > REQUESTED > ACCEPTED > RESERVED > MEETING ARRANGED >
  HANDOVER CONFIRMED > COMPLETED. Alternatives: REJECTED, CANCELLED, EXPIRED,
  DISPUTED.
SWAP: AVAILABLE > SWAP PROPOSED > COUNTERPROPOSED (optional) > MUTUALLY
  ACCEPTED > HANDOVER > BOTH PARTIES CONFIRM > COMPLETED.
BORROW: AVAILABLE > BORROW REQUESTED > APPROVED > RESERVED > COLLECTED >
  ACTIVE > RETURN INITIATED > BOTH PARTIES CONFIRM RETURN > COMPLETED.
RENT: AVAILABLE > RENTAL REQUESTED > APPROVED > RESERVED > COLLECTED >
  RENTAL ACTIVE > RETURN INITIATED > BOTH PARTIES CONFIRM RETURN > COMPLETED.

Rules: one active reservation per item for any overlapping period; prevent
double booking; no requests for unavailable items; validate rental and
borrowing dates; both parties see a clear status; cancellation under defined
conditions; record timestamps and WHO performed each confirmation; all state
transitions are server-side and validated; use database transactions where
several updates must succeed together.

Reservation expiry: when a seller accepts one of several interested buyers,
reserve the item temporarily, notify that buyer and give a confirmation
deadline. If it expires, release the item and notify the seller and eligible
waiting buyers. Never auto-select the next buyer without the seller's
consent. For borrowing and renting, expiry must respect availability dates and
overlapping reservations.

