SECTION 7: WANTED BOARD AND MATCHING
======================================================================
Extend the existing wanted board. A request has: item name, category,
description, max budget, desired condition, required-by date, preference
(BUY / BORROW / RENT / SWAP), optional duration for borrow/rent, and a status
(OPEN, PARTIALLY FULFILLED, FULFILLED, CLOSED, EXPIRED). Support an
"urgent" flag.

Rule-based matching service: when a request is created, search existing
available listings by category and item name, condition, budget or rental
constraints and availability, and return matches. When a listing is created,
find matching open requests, notify those students and show the matches to the
seller. Do not auto-close a request when one seller responds; the student
reviews alternatives and closes it manually. Use a simple, explainable
matching score (relevance, budget, condition, availability). No machine learning.

