SECTION 9: ANONYMOUS IDENTITY, VERIFICATION AND TRUST
======================================================================
Public profiles are pseudonymous: random username plus emoji avatar (for
example Panda_27 🐼, Mochi_14 🍡, Pixel_Fox 🦊). Users can change the avatar or
pick another available identity. Never expose real names, personal emails or
private account data publicly; keep an internal account identity for
authentication, transaction records and verification.

The existing app has no real authentication. Add lightweight demo
authentication (server-issued session/token). Every user-specific action must use
the SERVER-SIDE identity, never frontend-supplied user IDs. Clearly label demo
accounts as demo.

Verification: a campus verification mechanism (for example college-email
domain check with a simulated OTP, clearly labelled demo). A verified badge is
awarded only when that process succeeds. Do not auto-verify everyone.

Ratings: only after a COMPLETED transaction; buyer and seller can rate each
other (overall rating, optional short feedback, transaction reference);
prevent duplicates, ratings of incomplete transactions and self-rating.

Trust indicators: verification status, completed transactions, average
rating, successful swaps, rental/borrow history. Never show fabricated stats as
real achievements; label synthetic demo users.

